{
  "source": "scripts/color-taylor-script-cut-05.md",
  "wpm": 150,
  "gaps": {
    "line": 0.5,
    "paragraph": 1.2,
    "beat": 2.5
  },
  "lead": 3,
  "tail": 3,
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "1.1",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Hey, I'm Taylor, and I'm a real person.",
      "start": 3,
      "end": 6.2,
      "gapBefore": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "1.2",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "I'm also a user experience and product designer,",
      "start": 6.7,
      "end": 9.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.3",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "and I'd like to show you something I've been working on.",
      "start": 10.4,
      "end": 14.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.4",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "It's called Color Taylor.",
      "start": 15.3,
      "end": 16.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "1.5",
      "beat": 1,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "I'll just move myself out of the way, for now.",
      "start": 18.1,
      "end": 22.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.1",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "I used to struggle with picking colors using RGB.",
      "start": 24.6,
      "end": 28.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.2",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "In time, I found hue and saturation models were helpful for dialing in the colors I want.",
      "start": 28.7,
      "end": 35.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.3",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Let's say I have this turquoise,",
      "start": 36.7,
      "end": 39.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.4",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "but I want to get it to teal,",
      "start": 39.6,
      "end": 42.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.5",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "which is a harmonious, but darker color.",
      "start": 43.3,
      "end": 46.1,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.6",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "How do I dial that into RGB?",
      "start": 46.6,
      "end": 49.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.7",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "I think I need to lower the red",
      "start": 50.6,
      "end": 53.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.8",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "and the blue,",
      "start": 54.3,
      "end": 55.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.9",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "but how much do I change the RGB before I stray too far from my source?",
      "start": 56.7,
      "end": 63.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.10",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "Once I understood how hue models and RGB work together,",
      "start": 64.3,
      "end": 68.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.11",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "I could more confidently understand how colors were constructed.",
      "start": 68.8,
      "end": 72.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.12",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "There, that's teal.",
      "start": 73.6,
      "end": 74.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.13",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 13,
      "text": "Our focus for this presentation will be on hue, saturation, and brightness.",
      "start": 76,
      "end": 80.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.14",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 14,
      "text": "This app supports HSL as well, so you can use what's familiar to you.",
      "start": 81.3,
      "end": 86.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.15",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 15,
      "text": "Color Taylor is meant to be a playground and educational tool for how RGB and HSB work together.",
      "start": 88.1,
      "end": 95.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "2.16",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 16,
      "text": "You see the relationships in real time,",
      "start": 95.8,
      "end": 98.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "2.17",
      "beat": 2,
      "line": 17,
      "text": "which can strengthen your understanding of how colors work on displays.",
      "start": 99.1,
      "end": 103.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.1",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "The color editor on the right should be familiar to most people who have worked with creative tools.",
      "start": 106,
      "end": 113.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.2",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "The hexagon on the left is a different way of displaying the same information.",
      "start": 114.4,
      "end": 120,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.3",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Around the hexagon we have the Hue,",
      "start": 121.2,
      "end": 124,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.4",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "which is an angle that ranges from 0",
      "start": 124.5,
      "end": 127.7,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.5",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "to 360 degrees.",
      "start": 128.2,
      "end": 129.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.6",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Red is 0...",
      "start": 130.6,
      "end": 131.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.7",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "green is 120...",
      "start": 133,
      "end": 134.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.8",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "and blue is 240.",
      "start": 135.4,
      "end": 137,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.9",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "By laying the primary colors out like this,",
      "start": 138.2,
      "end": 141.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.10",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "we can visualize how RGB values determine a color's hue.",
      "start": 141.9,
      "end": 145.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.11",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "Drag the handles around and you see how",
      "start": 147.1,
      "end": 150.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.12",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "red, green, and blue combine to make a color.",
      "start": 150.8,
      "end": 154.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "3.13",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 13,
      "text": "You'll notice on the hexagon between each of the primary colors, we see combinations:",
      "start": 155.6,
      "end": 161.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.14",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 14,
      "text": "yellow, which is red and green combined;",
      "start": 162.4,
      "end": 165.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.15",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 15,
      "text": "cyan, which is green and blue combined;",
      "start": 166.4,
      "end": 169.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "3.16",
      "beat": 3,
      "line": 16,
      "text": "and magenta, which is blue and red combined.",
      "start": 170.4,
      "end": 173.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.1",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Let's use an orangey color as a reference point,",
      "start": 176.1,
      "end": 179.7,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.2",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Around 30 degrees we'll always have this warm tone between red and yellow.",
      "start": 180.9,
      "end": 186.1,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.3",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "At the highest saturation and brightness the color will be a combination of",
      "start": 187.3,
      "end": 192.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "4.4",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "2 parts red,",
      "start": 193,
      "end": 194.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.5",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "1 part green,",
      "start": 194.7,
      "end": 195.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "4.6",
      "beat": 4,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "0 parts blue.",
      "start": 196.4,
      "end": 197.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.1",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Saturation determines how colorful a color is.",
      "start": 200.1,
      "end": 202.9,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.2",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "100% saturation, like what we have here,",
      "start": 204.1,
      "end": 206.9,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.3",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "means the highest and lowest values are as far apart as they can be.",
      "start": 207.4,
      "end": 213,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.4",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Desaturating reduces the range between red, green, and blue proportionally.",
      "start": 214.2,
      "end": 218.2,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.5",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "When all three values are equal, there's no saturation, and you're left with gray.",
      "start": 219.4,
      "end": 225,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.6",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Adding saturation increases the range between values.",
      "start": 226.2,
      "end": 229,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.7",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "Saturation scales off the highest value.",
      "start": 230.2,
      "end": 232.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.8",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "For this orange, it's red, which holds still.",
      "start": 233.1,
      "end": 236.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.9",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "Green and blue move towards red or away from it",
      "start": 237.5,
      "end": 241.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.10",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "as we move the saturation slider.",
      "start": 242,
      "end": 244.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "5.11",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "Notice that the hue didn't change, only the range between RGB values changed.",
      "start": 245.6,
      "end": 250.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "5.12",
      "beat": 5,
      "line": 12,
      "text": "We're still at hue 30, which is the same orangey source color we started with.",
      "start": 251.3,
      "end": 257.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.1",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Brightness determines how light or dark a color is.",
      "start": 259.8,
      "end": 263.4,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.2",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "The highest RGB value sets the brightness.",
      "start": 264.6,
      "end": 267.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.3",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "As we adjust the brightness,",
      "start": 268.6,
      "end": 270.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.4",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "the hue and saturation are maintained.",
      "start": 271.1,
      "end": 273.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.5",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "This is done by scaling the RGB values proportionally off of zero.",
      "start": 274,
      "end": 278.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.6",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Brightness scales off of zero.",
      "start": 280,
      "end": 282,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.7",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "At 100% brightness the hexagon is at its largest.",
      "start": 283.2,
      "end": 286.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "6.8",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "As we lower the brightness, the hexagon contracts,",
      "start": 287.3,
      "end": 290.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.9",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 9,
      "text": "and red, green, and blue stems shorten with it,",
      "start": 291,
      "end": 294.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.10",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 10,
      "text": "keeping the same angles and proportions.",
      "start": 295.1,
      "end": 297.5,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "6.11",
      "beat": 6,
      "line": 11,
      "text": "Notice we stay at the same 30 degree orangey color while moving the brightness.",
      "start": 298,
      "end": 303.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.1",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "We'll use the swatches section to show how we can use HSB to set six different variations of the same hue.",
      "start": 306.1,
      "end": 314.5,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.2",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "We can use HSB to come up with a bright desaturated orange,",
      "start": 315.7,
      "end": 320.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "7.3",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "then go down the scale until we have a dark vibrant variant.",
      "start": 321,
      "end": 325.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "7.4",
      "beat": 7,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "This is hinting at what a design system might do.",
      "start": 327,
      "end": 331,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "8.1",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "We've been exploring the playground,",
      "start": 333.5,
      "end": 335.5,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.2",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "but if you want the classroom perspective,",
      "start": 336,
      "end": 338.8,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.3",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "check out the equations section.",
      "start": 339.3,
      "end": 341.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.4",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "It shows the math behind",
      "start": 342.5,
      "end": 344.5,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "8.5",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "hue,",
      "start": 345,
      "end": 345.4,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.6",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "saturation,",
      "start": 345.9,
      "end": 346.3,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.7",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 7,
      "text": "brightness,",
      "start": 346.8,
      "end": 347.2,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "8.8",
      "beat": 8,
      "line": 8,
      "text": "as well as how Hex and normalized colors are calculated.",
      "start": 348.4,
      "end": 352.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "9.1",
      "beat": 9,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Now we can move on to the demo.",
      "start": 354.9,
      "end": 358.1,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "10.1",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "Start with the sliders and controls you already know.",
      "start": 360.6,
      "end": 364.2,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "10.2",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "Moving one slider will highlight every other slider it affects.",
      "start": 365.4,
      "end": 369.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.3",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Click the droplet button to switch between source or mixed color sliders.",
      "start": 370.6,
      "end": 375.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.4",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Click the tags button to show HTML colors on the hexagon.",
      "start": 376.6,
      "end": 381,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.5",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Drag a handle on the hexagon and watch the RGB and HSB sliders follow.",
      "start": 382.2,
      "end": 387.8,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "10.6",
      "beat": 10,
      "line": 6,
      "text": "Have fun exploring and learning about different color models.",
      "start": 389,
      "end": 392.6,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.1",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 1,
      "text": "If you use Figma, I've also made a Color Taylor plugin that you might like to check out.",
      "start": 395.1,
      "end": 402.3,
      "gapBefore": 2.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.2",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 2,
      "text": "That's Color Taylor!",
      "start": 403.5,
      "end": 404.7,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.3",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 3,
      "text": "Go play with it, and I hope it helps you see the relationship between RGB and HSB in a different light.",
      "start": 405.2,
      "end": 413.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "If it's useful, I'd like to hear from you.",
      "start": 414.8,
      "end": 418.4,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.4",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 4,
      "text": "Questions and feedback are welcome.",
      "start": 418.9,
      "end": 420.9,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    },
    {
      "id": "11.5",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "Thanks for watching.",
      "start": 422.1,
      "end": 423.3,
      "gapBefore": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "11.5",
      "beat": 11,
      "line": 5,
      "text": "See ya.",
      "start": 423.8,
      "end": 424.6,
      "gapBefore": 0.5
    }
  ],
